g a pizza before heading back to our hotel. Literally stumbling onto Dante Pizza while looking for a slice, we walked in, waited our turn, and then ordered. They sell pizzas by the slice or whole pies if you're that drunk. My friend ordered a slice of cheese which wasn't ready but they promised it would be done in 2 minutes. I got a slice of pepperoni and a Coke. Total for a slice and a coke was $7, which is high, but understandable given t..."},{"business_id":"OqI87nbZ4s1ufOdvgAbgZw","review_id":"f_tY3BD5srtnEEmkRBzH2Q","date":"2015-03-30T10:26:06","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.924522876739502,"text_excerpt":"Best pizza in/around Bourbon street. I always frequent this place when I'm hungry after a night of drinking!"},{"business_id":"OqI87nbZ4s1ufOdvgAbgZw","review_id":"pk7waRj4xcROVy2tmlPLwg","date":"2018-01-05T20:43:09","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9228460788726807,"text_excerpt":"On New Years Eve day, it was only place where there wasn't a long line for lunch. It was so delicious. Great pizza and I highly recommend coming here"}],"visual":[{"business_id":"OqI87nbZ4s1ufOdvgAbgZw","photo_id":"ruC736OkkAWX0sqV4eaVaw","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/ruC736OkkAWX0sqV4eaVaw.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.9999998807907104}]},"notebook_case":null}
